<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacob Zuma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1942</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jacob Gedleyihlekisa Zuma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacob Zuma is a South African politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from 2009 to 2018 and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> from 2007 to 2017. A former anti-apartheid activist imprisoned on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robben-island">Robben Island</a>, he presided over a government marked by corruption and 'state capture', later investigated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zondo-commission">Zondo Commission</a>, and resigned under pressure from his party in 2018. In 2023 he launched the uMkhonto weSizwe party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacob-zuma.jpg" alt="Jacob Zuma" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Etienne Ansotte · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacob_Zuma,_29_November_2017_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
